.history/

# ---------- Local-only docs (NOT pushed to remote) ----------
# /docs/ is kept local — it contains the SRS PDF and other strategy
# material that doesn't belong in a public repo.
#
# EXCEPT docs/adr/. ADRs are decision records written to be read by the other
# two developers, and ignoring them made every ADR local to whichever machine
# wrote it: this clone holds 0002, 0006 and 0007 while comments in three
# middleware files cite an "ADR 0005" that does not exist here at all. Code
# comments across apps/api, apps/sadmin and packages/db now reference
# docs/adr/0007; a reference to a file teammates cannot open is worse than no
# reference. Note `/docs/*` rather than `/docs/` — git will not descend into an
# ignored DIRECTORY, so the negation below only works if the directory itself
# was never excluded. The SRS PDF and everything else under docs/ stay local.
/docs/*
!/docs/adr/
cookies.txt
_archived_routes/
